                      "fontFamily": "Inter",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "600",
                      "letterSpacing": 1.5
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "dgV3T",
                      "name": "todayReflText",
                      "fill": "$text-primary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Faith is not about having all the answers. It's about trusting the One who does. In our daily walk, we encounter moments of uncertainty, crossroads where the path forward isn't clear. It is in these very moments that our faith is refined.\n\nThe writer of Proverbs invites us to release our grip on self-sufficiency and instead lean into God's wisdom. This isn't passive surrender—it's an active choice to acknowledge God's sovereignty in every decision, every relationship, and every challenge we face.\n\nToday, consider the areas of your life where you've been relying solely on your own understanding. What would it look like to truly submit those areas to God?",
                      "lineHeight": 1.8,
                      "fontFamily": "Inter",
                      "fontSize": 16,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
